## Why This Is Asked
This question tests real-time monocular depth, multi-task learning, and pose estimation in a challenging forest domain, plus on-device few-shot adaptation and map fusion.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth and semantic/instance segmentation
- 6-DoF pose estimation for markers
- TSDF fusion for map building on edge hardware
- Differentiable rendering for domain adaptation
- On-device 5-shot adaptation with temporal consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture sketch
class MonocularDroneNet {
  constructor(){ /* backbone */ }
  forward(frame){
    const depth = this.depthHead(frameFeatures)
    const segPose = this.segPoseHead(frameFeatures)
    const pose = this.markerPoseHead(segPose)
    const map = this.tsdfFuse(depth, pose)
    return {depth, segPose, pose, map}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ablate temporal consistency vs per-frame independence?
- What data policies ensure robust marker generalization across weekly styles?
- How would you monitor edge latency under CPU/GPU contention?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses handling of articulated, hinge-based objects in clutter, real-time constraints, and on-device adaptation with few shots.

## Key Concepts

- Articulated 6-DoF pose estimation for hinged objects
- Hinge-state (open/closed) inference
- Synthetic+real data with domain adaptation
- Few-shot on-device fine-tuning
- Real-time edge deployment considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pose error metric example (illustrative)
function poseError(est, gt) {
  // est/gt: {R: rotation matrix, t: translation vector}
  const rotError = rotationDistance(est.R, gt.R);
  const transError = vectorDistance(est.t, gt.t);
  return { rotError, transError };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you mitigate pose ambiguity from symmetric trays?
- How would you extend to add new hinge geometries online without retraining a large model?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to handle equipment with strong reflective/transparent surfaces, a realistic industrial setting, and on-device adaptation under tight latency budgets.

## Key Concepts
- Reflective/transparent object pose estimation
- Differentiable rendering for photometric consistency
- On-device 3-shot adaptation via compact adapters
- Synthetic+real data with material randomization
- Edge latency and robustness under glare

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch
function forward(frame) {
  const feats = backbone(frame);
  const seg = segHead(feats);
  const pose = poseHead(feats);
  const render = differentiableRenderer(pose, frame);
  return {seg, pose, loss: computeLoss(render, frame)};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt to varying refractive indices?
- How would you quantify uncertainty in pose under specular highlights?

## Why This Is Asked
Introduces a new angle: multi-sensor fusion with event cameras for high-dynamic scenes. Assesses architectural discipline and concrete trade-offs for low latency and on-device adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Event cameras and RGB fusion
- 3D voxel grids and lightweight transformers
- On-device 5-shot adaptation and object priors
- Temporal consistency and occlusion handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code: fuse RGB features with events, then predict pose and mask
function forward(rgbFrame, events, priors){
  const rgbFeat = rgbBackbone(rgbFrame);
  const evtFeat = eventBackbone(events);
  const fused = fuse3D(rgbFeat, evtFeat);
  const pose = poseHead(fused, priors);
  const mask = segHead(fused);
  return {pose, mask};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design synthetic data generation to cover unseen shapes with realistic event streams?
- What debugging metrics would help you diagnose latency vs. accuracy bottlenecks on edge hardware?

